/italic> = 109) in postmenopausal women from Qu&#x000e9;bec, Canada.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-001429f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-ehp0115-001429" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Correlations between plasma concentrations of the &#x02211;PBDEs and relative contributions of PBDE-47 (<italic>A;</italic> Pearson&#x02019;s <italic>r</italic> = 0.22; <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.026) and PBDE-153 (<italic>B;</italic> Pearson&#x02019;s <italic>r</italic> = 0.49; <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.001) to the &#x02211;PBDE levels in 110 postmenopausal women from Qu&#x000e9;bec, Canada.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp0115-001429f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ehp0115-001429" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Selected characteristics of the 110 postmenopausal women, Qu&#x000e9;bec, Canada.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristic</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No. (%)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mean &#x000b1; SD</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age (years)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">58.3 &#x000b1; 5.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48 to 76</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Weight (kg)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">68.7 &#x000b1; 14.0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">44.8 to 133.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Height (cm)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">160 &#x000b1; 5.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">146 to 172</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BMI (kg/m<sup>2</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan=